{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And the waters returned.</b> Below the earth as is their norm, at the end of one hundred and fifty days. This calculation too — by way of prophecy they knew. And those who say: behold, we find one hundred and fifty days, five months — this is for us a sign that they are solar months — behold, they have not spoken accurately in their own words, for two days are missing. Also the one who says that it was by the calculation of intercalation, and would place it in the second month of Marcheshvan, and make the year full — and why all this? Even if it were written that Noah's calculation was by the sun, or that the beginning of the year was from Tishrei — the appointed times were not given through Noah. And it is even possible regarding the resting of the ark to speak lengthy words — therefore they are of no avail and do not save, for they are confusion:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The comment cuts off with 'כי תהו המה' ('for they are confusion/confusion are they'), apparently the end of this comment; the syntax of the final clause is elliptical and has been rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:46.759000153Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}